! [PrimaryClaim] the pure receipt revision is necessary and sufficient before M2C can represent physical root continuity honestly
  @ [support] the selected source identifies missing root identity and stable final-path fields
  @ [support] the root reconciliation research requires both fields at receipt issuance
  @ [support] no physical API or truth check is needed to validate their syntax
  + [confidence] is high for pure schema sufficiency and intentionally none for physical correspondence

& [Problem] is an under-bound receipt and invalid authority identity
  + [physical_gap] old receipts do not name the root StrongFileIdentity or stable volume-GUID final path
  + [semantic_gap] one profile field conflates receipt schema with scanner policy
  + [governance_gap] the prior specification names a non-governing satisfaction-protocol UUID
  + [consequence] a future scanner could emit structurally valid evidence that does not commit the physical root object it observed

& [WhyPureRevision] is dependency order
  + [M2C_dependency] physical scanner output cannot be designed truthfully until its receipt schema can express root continuity
  + [fail_early] malformed and weak evidence should reject before platform calls or supervisor integration exist
  + [low_risk] the change has no I/O, unsafe, dependency, persistence, or migration surface
  + [compiler_value] a breaking Rust field change exposes all internal construction sites

& [WhyRejectLegacy] is security and honesty
  + [weakness] the old shape lacks facts that cannot be reconstructed from its serialized fields
  + [consumer_state] no scanner, ledger, persisted receipt, or external consumer exists
  + [cost] a legacy decoder would permanently admit a second weaker evidence contract
  + [decision] strict missing-field and unknown-field rejection is the smallest truthful compatibility policy

& [WhySeparateProfiles] is data identity
  + [forms] changes when the pure public vocabulary changes
  + [receipt] changes when the serialized receipt contract changes
  + [scanner] changes only when physical observation policy changes
  + [benefit] later evolution can invalidate exactly the affected contract without semantic aliasing

& [WhyVolumeGuidSyntax] is stable evidence without overclaim
  + [value] a future scanner can record the normalized handle-derived namespace independently of the human reopen address
  + [strictness] a closed lowercase GUID grammar avoids multiple spellings of the same evidence identity
  + [preservation] tail text remains exact and is never case-folded or Unicode-normalized
  + [limit] pure validation cannot prove existence, locality, NTFS, or correspondence to root_identity

& [Counterarguments] are resolved
  + [keep_profile] is rejected because the field cannot identify both schema and policy without ambiguity
  + [optional_root_fields] is rejected because optional evidence recreates the original defect
  + [default_root_fields] is rejected because defaults fabricate observation
  + [validate_physical_match] is deferred because it requires the separately governed M2C effect boundary
  + [normalize_tail] is rejected because it mutates the evidence string and can damage Unicode or case

& [InvalidationConditions] are explicit
  + [unexpected_consumer] is a real persisted or external 0.1 receipt consumer discovered before implementation
  + [source_change] is correction source or preserved snapshot alteration
  + [grammar_contradiction] is primary API evidence that normalized volume-GUID output cannot satisfy the closed grammar
  + [implementation_contradiction] is a required field or validation rule that cannot remain pure
  + [quality_failure] is any focused, global, evidence, or registry gate failure
  = must: stop and reprocess rather than weakening the canonical specification in place

& [FileChangeScope] is bounded
  + [production] is crates\cantor_ecosystem\src\topology_forms.rs
  + [tests] are the same module and its existing evidence integration test
  + [governance] is source manifest, exploded, canonical, justification, plan, matrix, slice, registry, solution, proof, turn, fault, file-change, documentation, and evidence manifest
  + [dependency] is unchanged
  + [public_export] is unchanged because topology_forms is already exported

& [VerificationJustification] is defense in depth
  + [unit] proves profiles, field presence, identity, grammar, old-shape rejection, and exact round trip
  + [static] proves no forbidden import, unsafe, or dependency drift
  + [global] proves no regression across all workspace consumers
  + [evidence] binds source, authority, implementation, tests, proof, and predecessor manifests

& [Rollback] is zero-migration
  + [action] revert the schema implementation and governed artifacts to commit aac126e
  + [state] no durable receipt data exists
  + [condition] rollback is allowed only before any M2C consumer is admitted
  - never: roll back by accepting old receipts as equivalent to strengthened receipts
